            <ArticleTitle>Case 3: Insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>916, A10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dyslipidemia secondary to insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus is common among patients whose plasma glucose levels are poorly controlled. Because of the high mortality associated with diabetes, prompt intervention to correct the dyslipidemia is warranted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
